Some parts of these apps are not the authors' to license and are not covered by
the licence above; the first three are described in running-dashboard/TILES.md:

- The map tiles under running-dashboard/data/tiles/ are from USGS The National Map,
  a work of the United States government in the public domain.
- The route shapes in scripts/demo_courses.json, and the demo session streams
  derived from them under running-dashboard/data/, are derived from OpenStreetMap
  data, © OpenStreetMap contributors, and are made available under the Open
  Database License (ODbL) 1.0.
- The Geist typeface in running-dashboard/fonts/ is © Vercel, licensed under the
  SIL Open Font License 1.1 (running-dashboard/fonts/LICENSE-Geist.txt).
- The anatomical geometry under anatomy/data/ is derived from BodyParts3D,
  © The Database Center for Life Science (DBCLS), licensed CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan
  (the source is now also published under CC BY 4.0), and the adapted geometry is
  shared under the same licence — see anatomy/CREDITS.txt. anatomy/vendor/ is
  three.js under the MIT licence (anatomy/vendor/three-LICENSE.txt); the fonts
  under anatomy/fonts/ are Atkinson Hyperlegible and Newsreader under the SIL
  Open Font License 1.1 (anatomy/fonts/OFL.txt).
- The reservoir model under norne-reservoir/data/ is derived from the Norne
  benchmark case published through the Open Porous Media initiative, and is a
  derived database under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — see
  norne-reservoir/data/ATTRIBUTION.txt. The topside layer in
  norne-reservoir/data/topside.json and topside-network.json contains data
  under the Norwegian licence for Open Government data (NLOD) distributed by
  the Norwegian Offshore Directorate (Sokkeldirektoratet) — FactMaps and
  FactPages — re-centred, rounded and re-projected as ATTRIBUTION.txt states;
  its coastline is Natural Earth, public domain.
- The terrain under besseggen/data/ is derived from Kartverket's Nasjonal
  høydemodell (DTM1), © Kartverket, under NLOD 2.0 and CC BY 4.0; the trail from
  Kartverket's Turrutebasen (open data, no conditions); the lakes, rivers and
  glaciers from N50 Kartdata, © Kartverket, CC BY 4.0; the place names from the
  Sentralt stedsnavnregister (SSR), © Kartverket, CC BY 4.0 — each with its
  adaptations described in besseggen/CREDITS.txt. besseggen/vendor/ is three.js
  under the MIT licence and besseggen/fonts/ are Atkinson Hyperlegible and
  Newsreader under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (besseggen/fonts/OFL.txt).
- The wind and weather fields under global-wind/data/ and global-weather/data/
  are NOAA Global Forecast System output, a work of the United States government
  in the public domain. The coastlines in both apps' assets/world.json are
  Natural Earth, public domain; the city labels in assets/places.json are
  © GeoNames under CC BY 4.0, whose attribution is a condition of use; and
  assets/fflate.min.js is fflate under the MIT licence — see
  global-wind/assets/LICENSES.md and global-weather/assets/LICENSES.md.
- The data under milky-way/data/ is adapted from the sources listed, with their
  licences and adaptations, in milky-way/CREDITS.txt. The planet, moon and
  rotation data are from JPL/NAIF (freely available SPICE data). The asteroid
  and comet orbits are from the JPL Small-Body Database, the Minor Planet
  Center and ESA's NEO Coordination Centre, under their terms as quoted there.
  The planet and moon maps are NASA and USGS products: public domain, except
  that the New Horizons Pluto map states no licence and the Cassini Jupiter map
  is under JPL's image use policy. The galaxy layer uses the
  Local Volume Database (CC0 1.0), galstreams (BSD 3-Clause), SpiralMap (MIT)
  and Agama (BSD/MIT), whose full licence texts close milky-way/CREDITS.txt.
  The exoplanets are from the Open Exoplanet Catalogue (MIT).
  - milky-way/data/tex/sun.jpg, milky-way/data/tex/moon.jpg and
    milky-way/data/stars/constellations.json are adapted from Stellarium under
    CC BY-SA 4.0 and are shared under the same licence.
  - milky-way/data/stars/deep.bin and milky-way/data/stars/named.json are
    adapted from AT-HYG and HYG (CC BY-SA 4.0).
  - Those two files, milky-way/data/sky/gaia-dr3-counts.jpg and
    milky-way/data/galaxy/young-*.png contain data from the European Space
    Agency mission Gaia, processed by the Gaia Data Processing and Analysis
    Consortium (DPAC). That data is licensed under CC BY-NC 3.0 IGO, so these
    files may be used for non-commercial purposes only.
  - The young-star maps, milky-way/data/galaxy/young-gaiadr3-ob.png and
    milky-way/data/galaxy/young-poggio2021-ums.png, are taken from SpiralMap,
    which includes them with their authors' permission. That permission was
    given to SpiralMap; no separate grant to downstream redistributors was
    found.
  - milky-way/vendor/ is three.js under the MIT licence
    (milky-way/vendor/three-LICENSE.txt), and milky-way/fonts/ are Atkinson
    Hyperlegible and Newsreader under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
    (milky-way/fonts/OFL.txt).
- The North Sea data under shelf-atlas/data/ and the world data under
  world-oil-gas/data/ are adapted (datum-shifted, simplified, unit-converted,
  packed) from the sources listed with their licences in shelf-atlas/RESEARCH.md
  and on each app's attribution screen:
  - Norway: contains data under the Norwegian licence for Open Government data
    (NLOD) distributed by the Norwegian Offshore Directorate (FactPages,
    FactMaps shapefiles).
  - United Kingdom: contains information provided by the North Sea Transition
    Authority and/or other third parties, under the NSTA Open User Licence
    (June 2023), which permits copying, publishing, adapting and
    non-commercial exploitation only.
  - Denmark: Danish Energy Agency production reports and field delineations,
    and the Agency's installations list via GEUS; no licence is stated at the
    source, and reuse here rests on the Danish PSI Act with attribution.
  - Netherlands: NLOG (TNO) field, facility and production data; NLOG claims
    no intellectual property rights in the data it provides.
  - Marine Regions Maritime Boundaries v12, Flanders Marine Institute (2023),
    CC BY 4.0; EMODnet Human Activities pipelines, CC BY 4.0; Natural Earth
    coastline, countries and bathymetry, public domain.
  - Our World in Data's energy dataset (Energy Institute Statistical Review of
    World Energy and The Shift Data Portal), CC BY 4.0.
  - Global Energy Monitor's Global Oil and Gas Extraction Tracker, when
    dropped into world-oil-gas/raw/manual/ and built into
    world-oil-gas/data/fields.json, CC BY 4.0.
